        "answer": {
          "short": "Both are $4096$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}(2^3)^4&=8^4\\\\&=4096\\\\(2^6)^2&=64^2\\\\&=4096\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p68-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Explain why they are the same",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The bases are the same, and $3\\times4=6\\times2=12$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}(2^3)^4&=2^{3\\times4}\\\\&=2^{12}\\\\(2^6)^2&=2^{6\\times2}\\\\&=2^{12}\\end{aligned}$$\n\nBoth expressions have the same base and the same final index.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
