        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Correct answer: A, B, C.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{A: }(2^4)^3&=2^{12}\\\\\\text{B: }(2^2)^6&=2^{12}\\\\\\text{C: }(4^2)^3&=4^6\\\\&=2^{12}\\\\\\text{D: }(4^3)^2\\times(6^2)^2&=2^{12}\\times6^4\\end{aligned}$$D has an extra factor of $6^4$, so it is not equal to $2^{12}$. Correct answer: A, B, C.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
